        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148321,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wenn wir jedes Element in einem Array ändern und das Ergebnis in einem neuen Array speichern wollten, wie könnten wir das tun?</p><p>Eine Möglichkeit, dies zu tun, besteht darin, eine Schleife zu verwenden, um Werte vor dem Speichern zu konvertieren. Das funktioniert, aber JavaScript hat eine noch bessere Lösung.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"array\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"97\" endIndex=\"108\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = [];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element \" /><text value=\"of\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" d = \" /><text value=\"Math\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".max(\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", element - \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage.push(d);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>enemyDamage</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148322,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JavaScript hat eine praktische Funktion namens <code>.map()</code>, die, wenn sie auf ein Array angewendet wird, es uns ermöglicht, jeden Wert zu ändern und in einem neuen Array zu speichern.</p><p><code>.map()</code> folgt der Syntax: <code>arrayName.map()</code>. Schauen wir uns an, wie wir es auf das <code>enemyDamage</code>-Array anwenden können.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"reducedDamage\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"82\" /><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"83\" /><option startIndex=\"83\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"88\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map();\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>enemyDamage</code>, gefolgt von <code>.</code> und schließlich <code>map</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>;</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148323,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um <code>.map()</code> mitzuteilen, wie jedes Element modifiziert werden soll, müssen wir eine Funktion als Parameter übergeben.</p><p>Später werden wir unsere Änderungen in diese Funktion programmieren.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"95\" /><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"96\" /><option startIndex=\"96\" endIndex=\"97\" /><option startIndex=\"98\" endIndex=\"99\" /><option startIndex=\"99\" endIndex=\"100\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>function</code>, gefolgt von <code>(</code> und schließlich <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148324,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Bevor wir die Array-Werte ändern können, müssen wir sie an die Funktion übergeben. Das machen wir, indem wir der Inline-Funktion einen Parameter hinzufügen.</p><p>In unserem Beispiel nennen wir den Parameter <code>element</code>, aber jeder Name kann funktionieren.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"86\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"56\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"27\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"38\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" bonusUnlocked = scores.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (element % \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\") == \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(bonusUnlocked);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>element</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148325,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Das Hinzufügen eines zweiten Parameters ermöglicht es uns, auf den Index jeder Iteration zusammen mit dem Array-Wert zuzugreifen.</p><p>In unserem Beispiel nennen wir den Parameter <code>index</code>, aber jeder Name kann funktionieren.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"113\" endIndex=\"118\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" inventory = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Shield&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Key&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" displayInventory = inventory.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" index + \" /><text value=\"&quot;: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(displayInventory);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>index</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148326,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um der <code>.map()</code>-Funktion mitzuteilen, welchen Wert sie im neuen Array speichern soll, muss die Inline-Funktion einen Wert <code>return</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"108\" endIndex=\"114\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Math\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".max(\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", element - \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>return</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148327,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um unsere Syntax zu vereinfachen, können wir die Inline-Funktion stattdessen durch eine JavaScript-Arrow-Funktion ersetzen.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"132\" endIndex=\"139\" /><option startIndex=\"141\" endIndex=\"143\" /><option startIndex=\"144\" endIndex=\"165\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" spriteNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;hero_idle&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;slime_walk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;coin_spin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;door_open&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;boss_roar&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" uppercaseSprites = \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" spriteNames.map(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" element.toUpperCase());\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(uppercaseSprites);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>element</code>, gefolgt von <code>=&gt;</code> und schließlich <code>element.toUpperCase()</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148328,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>.map()</code> funktioniert nicht nur mit Integer-Arrays, sondern auch mit anderen Werttypen, wie zum Beispiel Strings.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Array\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"this\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"90\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;goblin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;hannah&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;dragon&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" nameLength =\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" enemyNames.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element.length;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(nameLength);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>enemyNames</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148329,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Welche JavaScript-Funktion können wir verwenden, um jedes Element zu modifizieren und die Ergebnisse in einem neuen Array zu speichern?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\"><code>.map()</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>.convert()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>.map()</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148330,
            "contentType": "interactive",
